{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat judging-v13-draft.txt'","aggregated_output":"You are a senior hedge-fund analyst judging the current rungs of a family of related number theses: one company's quantities that overlap, such as a total and its segment, a level and its growth, or a later year that rests on an earlier year's base. Use only the supplied evidence and themes in force. Each rung is your forecast: the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved.\n\n- Rejudge every member from the evidence shown (what recent judgements relied on and what arrived recently) and the themes in force. Pieces in force that no recent judgement relied on are not shown; each member's earlier forecast reflects them, but its figures are our own, never a source and never the market's expectation. Do not add to or subtract from a previous score. The earlier forecasts are supplied only for comparison.\n- Judge each member against a reference: what the market expects for that question (consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline). Say where the reference sits on its ladder. A consensus or guidance figure by itself keeps the judgement at the reference's rung; once other evidence has arrived it is never the reason to stay. Then derive the outcome the evidence implies: reported figures and guidance give a run-rate that carries the guided growth forward, never the last quarter annualised flat; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it. A target for a product with no shipments yet is discounted by default; it is taken in full only when the evidence shows the volume in hand. Build the family's figures once and read every member's outcome from them: a part cannot exceed its whole, a figure that spans several periods or products gives a question only its share, and a quantity the family shares has one forecast per scenario. Compare each outcome with its rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.\n- Weigh by tier and by novelty. Only fact can establish that a rung's outcome already holds; \"not established\" is a statement of confidence, never a reason to stay. Guidance for the current or next quarter is the strongest forecast input. A management target for a product not yet shipping, or an ambition spanning years, is an input to be discounted for time and execution (how many selling quarters remain, what volume and price the figure implies, what the company's own choices say), not an answer; consensus is where the market stands, not the answer either. third_party_view and rumour move the forecast in proportion to their specificity (a number, a date, a named party): a research firm's shipment or revenue tracking with a number counts. A commitment or deal that is announced but not sized is sized from its disclosed comparable (the same programme's other deal, scaled by capacity or units); a figure no one states is derived from the accounting identities in the evidence when they allow it. A repeat, another outlet for the same claim, or an opinion that adds no new fact or calculation moves nothing. Missing confirmation alone is not grounds for the lowest or highest rung: an event not being confirmed is not confirmation that it did not happen.\n- An evidence item that replaces another includes its predecessor for context, such as guidance revised from 12% to 25% growth. The predecessor is no longer evidence in force.\n- \"Themes in force\" lists the library's open theme theses (policy stages, shared quantities) with their current conclusions. They are our own judgements, never evidence: do not cite them in cites. Weigh each one that bears on a member and report it in that member's theme_pushes with the direction it pushes that member (toward_first, toward_last or none); leave out a theme that does not bear on it. A theme marked \"updated since this thesis was last judged\" may change the conclusion; one that is not marked already stood at the previous judgement. When no themes are listed, theme_pushes is empty.\n- Your conclusions must be consistent with each other and with the themes in force as shown: a share cannot be judged at zero while the policy that gates it is judged likely to open.\n- Return the family's figures and one answer per member, as the JSON schema defines them. Every number an answer rests on is a figure; a number you judge rather than read or compute is an estimate, stated as yours. When the evidence cannot support a member's forecast, answer it unresolved and say why. Write explanations in English; preserve IDs and any quoted source text.\n- changed is true for a different rung or a change to the key facts or figures supporting the same rung, including a changed implied outcome. Repetition or another source for the same statement does not alone change the conclusion. A first judgement always has changed true.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba render_v13.py | sed -n '15,151p'\"","aggregated_output":"    15\t\n    16\tS, N = {'type': 'string'}, {'type': 'number'}\n    17\t\n    18\t\n    19\tdef nullable(schema):\n    20\t    return {'anyOf': [schema, {'type': 'null'}]}\n    21\t\n    22\t\n    23\tdef obj(props, desc=None):\n    24\t    out = {'type': 'object', 'properties': props, 'required': list(props), 'additionalProperties': False}\n    25\t    if desc:\n    26\t        out['description'] = desc\n    27\t    return out\n    28\t\n    29\t\n    30\tdef v13_schema(member_ids, evidence_ids, theme_ids):\n    31\t    what = obj({k: S for k in ('population', 'measure', 'scope', 'period')},\n    32\t               'What the number measures: population, measure (the quantity, such as revenue or units; never its basis), scope, period.')\n    33\t    figure = obj({\n    34\t        'id': S, 'what': what,\n    35\t        'basis': {'type': 'string', 'enum': sorted(cc.BASES), 'description': 'reported: an actual; guidance: the company\\'s outlook; consensus: '\n    36\t                  'analysts\\' average; third_party: one outside party; forecast: this family\\'s forecast; prior_forecast: our earlier forecast.'},\n    37\t        'scenario': S,\n    38\t        'kind': {'type': 'string', 'enum': sorted(cc.KINDS), 'description': 'source: stated in a shown passage; computed: one operation on '\n    39\t                 'named figures; estimate: your judgement, stated as yours; prior: our earlier forecast, for comparison only.'},\n    40\t        'value': nullable(N), 'low': nullable(N), 'high': nullable(N),\n    41\t        'bound': nullable({'type': 'string', 'enum': ['>', '>=', '<', '<=', 'approx', 'approx_below', 'approx_above']}),\n    42\t        'unit': S,\n    43\t        'evidence': nullable(S),\n    44\t        'expression': nullable({'type': 'string', 'description': 'Source only: the complete numeric expression exactly as the passage writes '\n    45\t                                'it, qualifiers included (for example \"more than $2 billion\", \"$4.5 billion, plus or minus 3%\", \"more than triple\").'}),\n    46\t        'component': nullable({'type': 'string', 'enum': ['value', 'bound', 'midpoint', 'relative', 'low', 'high', 'multiplier']}),\n    47\t        'inputs': nullable({'type': 'array', 'items': S}),\n    48\t        'operation': nullable({'type': 'string', 'enum': sorted(cc.OPERATIONS)}),\n    49\t        'signs': nullable({'type': 'array', 'items': N}),\n    50\t        'relation': nullable({'type': 'string', 'enum': ['time_aggregation', 'accounting_parts', 'stated_in_addition', 'overlap_unknown'],\n    51\t                              'description': 'Sum and roll_forward: periods of one quantity; declared parts of a whole; a source says they add; '\n    52\t                              'unknown overlap (name the disputed figure).'}),\n    53\t        'disputed': nullable(S),\n    54\t        'bridge': nullable({'type': 'string', 'description': 'Only when no listed identity covers the operation (periods of one quantity, '\n    55\t                            'declared parts, a balance and its flows, a stated share or multiplier, a total over a per-unit price): an '\n    56\t                            'estimate stating the conversion and listing the operands it converts.'}),\n    57\t        'basis_text': nullable(S), 'rests_on': nullable({'type': 'array', 'items': S}),\n    58\t        'adjusts': nullable(obj({'figure': S, 'type': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['discount', 'uplift', 'trim']}})),\n    59\t        'converts': nullable({'type': 'array', 'items': S}),\n    60\t        'pointer': nullable(obj({'view': S, 'day': S})),\n    61\t    })\n    62\t    push = obj({'evidence_id': {'type': 'string', 'enum': evidence_ids}, 'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['toward_first', 'toward_last', 'none']}})\n    63\t    theme_push = obj({'view_id': {'type': 'string', 'enum': theme_ids or ['none']},\n    64\t                      'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['toward_first', 'toward_last', 'none']}})\n    65\t    answer = obj({\n    66\t        'view_id': {'type': 'string', 'enum': member_ids},\n    67\t        'shape': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['forecast', 'unresolved']},\n    68\t        'outcome': nullable(S), 'rung': nullable({'type': 'integer'}),\n    69\t        'reference': nullable(obj({'figure': nullable(S), 'unavailable': nullable(S)}, 'An external figure, or a calculation from external '\n    70\t                              'and reported figures, or unavailable with why; never our earlier forecast.')),\n    71\t        'reasons': S, 'why': nullable(S),\n    72\t        'cites': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string', 'enum': evidence_ids}},\n    73\t        'pushes': {'type': 'array', 'items': push}, 'theme_pushes': {'type': 'array', 'items': theme_push},\n    74\t        'changed': {'type': 'boolean'}, 'why_changed': S,\n    75\t    })\n    76\t    return obj({'figures': {'type': 'array', 'items': figure}, 'answers': {'type': 'array', 'items': answer}})\n    77\t\n    78\t\n    79\tdef parts(user):\n    80\t    head, rest = user.split('\\n\\n[Evidence in view', 1)\n    81\t    evidence = '[Evidence in view' + rest.split('\\n\\n[', 1)[0]\n    82\t    tail = '\\n\\n[' + rest.split('\\n\\n[', 1)[1] if '\\n\\n[' in rest else ''\n    83\t    blocks = {b.split(']', 1)[0]: '[' + b for b in tail.split('\\n\\n[')[1:]}\n    84\t    return head, evidence, blocks\n    85\t\n    86\t\n    87\tdef render(archive_path, calls, family):\n    88\t    archive = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{archive_path}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    89\t    heads, lines, seen, themes, earlier = [], [], set(), '', []\n    90\t    for view_id, call_id in calls:\n    91\t        user = json.loads(archive.execute('select request_json from model_calls where call_id=?', (call_id,)).fetchone()[0])['messages'][1]['content']\n    92\t        head, evidence, blocks = parts(user)\n    93\t        heads.append(head)\n    94\t        for item in evidence.split('\\n- ')[1:]:\n    95\t            eid = item.split(' ', 1)[0]\n    96\t            if eid not in seen:\n    97\t                seen.add(eid)\n    98\t                lines.append('- ' + item)\n    99\t        themes = themes or next((v for k, v in blocks.items() if k.startswith('Themes')), '')\n   100\t        prev = next((v for k, v in blocks.items() if k.startswith('Previous')), '').split('\\n\\nAnswer per the JSON schema')[0]   # [46g.1] v7's output line goes\n   101\t        earlier.append(f'- {view_id}: ' + prev.replace('[Previous conclusion, for comparison only]', 'our earlier forecast, not a source:').strip())\n   102\t    rel = '; '.join(f'{r[\"part\"]} is part of {r[\"whole\"]}' for r in family['relations'] if r['type'] == 'part_of')\n   103\t    shared = '; '.join(f'{w[\"population\"]}, {w[\"measure\"]}, {w[\"scope\"]}, {w[\"period\"]}' for w in family['shared'])\n   104\t    user = ('[Family] members:\\n' + '\\n\\n'.join(heads) + f'\\n\\nRelations: {rel}.\\nShared quantities, one forecast each per scenario: {shared}.\\n\\n'\n   105\t            f'[Evidence in view for the family, {len(lines)} items]\\n' + '\\n'.join(lines) + '\\n\\n' + themes + '\\n\\n[Earlier forecasts]\\n'\n   106\t            + '\\n'.join(earlier) + '\\n\\nAnswer per the JSON schema: one calculation for the family and one answer per member.')\n   107\t    return user, sorted(seen), [t.split(' ', 1)[0] for t in themes.split('\\n- ')[1:]]\n   108\t\n   109\t\n   110\tdef strict(calc, schema):\n   111\t    \"\"\"Fill every optional field with null, as strict structured output returns it.\"\"\"\n   112\t    fprops = schema['properties']['figures']['items']['properties']\n   113\t    aprops = schema['properties']['answers']['items']['properties']\n   114\t    figs = [{k: f.get(k) for k in fprops} for f in calc['figures']]\n   115\t    for f in figs:\n   116\t        f['scenario'] = f['scenario'] or 'base'\n   117\t        if f['what'] is None:\n   118\t            f['what'] = {'population': '', 'measure': '', 'scope': '', 'period': ''}\n   119\t    answers = []\n   120\t    for a in calc['answers']:\n   121\t        a2 = {k: a.get(k) for k in aprops}\n   122\t        if a2['reference'] is not None:\n   123\t            a2['reference'] = {'figure': a['reference'].get('figure'), 'unavailable': a['reference'].get('unavailable')}\n   124\t        a2['why'] = a.get('why')\n   125\t        answers.append(a2)\n   126\t    return {'figures': figs, 'answers': answers}\n   127\t\n   128\t\n   129\tdef without_nulls(calc):\n   130\t    clean = lambda d: {k: v for k, v in d.items() if v is not None}\n   131\t    answers = []\n   132\t    for a in calc['answers']:\n   133\t        a2 = clean(a)\n   134\t        if 'reference' in a2:\n   135\t            a2['reference'] = clean(a2['reference'])\n   136\t        answers.append(a2)\n   137\t    return {'figures': [clean(f) for f in calc['figures']], 'answers': answers}\n   138\t\n   139\t\n   140\tdef main():\n   141\t    archive = REPO / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/archive.sqlite'\n   142\t    system = (HERE / 'judging-v13-draft.txt').read_text()\n   143\t    user, evidence_ids, theme_ids = render(archive, [('v14', 8729), ('v9', 8737)], gate.R1_FAMILY)\n   144\t    schema = v13_schema(['v14', 'v9'], evidence_ids, theme_ids)\n   145\t    calc = gate.r1('c')\n   146\t    answer = strict(calc, schema)\n   147\t    schema_errors = model.check_schema(answer, schema)\n   148\t    for a in answer['answers']:\n   149\t        a['cites'] = [e for e in a['cites'] if e in evidence_ids]\n   150\t    result = cc.check(gate.R1_FAMILY, gate.R1_PASSAGES, without_nulls(answer))\n   151\t    missing = sorted({f['evidence'] for f in calc['figures'] if f.get('evidence')} - set(evidence_ids))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba calc_check.py | sed -n '160,265p;310,455p'\"","aggregated_output":"   160\t\n   161\tdef _close(declared, expected, unit):\n   162\t    floor = 0.05 if unit == '%' else 0.1\n   163\t    return abs(declared - expected) <= max(0.005 * abs(expected), floor)\n   164\t\n   165\t\n   166\tQUARTERS = {'Q1': {1}, 'Q2': {2}, 'Q3': {3}, 'Q4': {4}, 'H1': {1, 2}, 'H2': {3, 4}}\n   167\t\n   168\t\n   169\tdef _quarters(period):\n   170\t    \"\"\"'FY2027' -> (FY2027, {1..4}); 'FY2027 Q3' -> (FY2027, {3}); 'FY2027 H1' -> {1, 2}; else None.\"\"\"\n   171\t    parts = period.split()\n   172\t    if len(parts) == 1 and parts[0].startswith('FY'):\n   173\t        return parts[0], {1, 2, 3, 4}\n   174\t    if len(parts) == 2 and parts[0].startswith('FY') and parts[1] in QUARTERS:\n   175\t        return parts[0], QUARTERS[parts[1]]\n   176\t    return None\n   177\t\n   178\t\n   179\tdef _key(what):\n   180\t    return (what['population'], what['measure'], what['scope'], what['period'])\n   181\t\n   182\t\n   183\tdef check(family, passages, calc):\n   184\t    errors, recorded = [], []\n   185\t    figs = {}\n   186\t    for fig in calc['figures']:\n   187\t        if fig['id'] in figs:\n   188\t            errors.append(('C7', f'{fig[\"id\"]} is defined twice'))\n   189\t        figs[fig['id']] = fig\n   190\t\n   191\t    def refs(fig):\n   192\t        out = list(fig.get('inputs', []))\n   193\t        out += [r for r in fig.get('rests_on', []) if r in figs or r not in passages]\n   194\t        if fig.get('adjusts'):\n   195\t            out.append(fig['adjusts']['figure'])\n   196\t        if fig.get('bridge'):\n   197\t            out.append(fig['bridge'])\n   198\t        return out\n   199\t\n   200\t    # C7 structure: kinds, operations, dangling, cycles\n   201\t    for fig in figs.values():\n   202\t        if fig.get('kind') not in KINDS or fig.get('basis') not in BASES:\n   203\t            errors.append(('C7', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: kind {fig.get(\"kind\")} or basis {fig.get(\"basis\")} outside the closed set'))\n   204\t        if fig.get('kind') == 'computed' and fig.get('operation') not in OPERATIONS:\n   205\t            errors.append(('C7', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: operation {fig.get(\"operation\")} outside the closed set'))\n   206\t        for r in refs(fig):\n   207\t            if r not in figs:\n   208\t                errors.append(('C7', f'{fig[\"id\"]} refers to {r}, which is not defined'))\n   209\t    state = {}\n   210\t\n   211\t    def cyclic(fid):\n   212\t        if state.get(fid) == 1:\n   213\t            return True\n   214\t        if state.get(fid) == 2 or fid not in figs:\n   215\t            return False\n   216\t        state[fid] = 1\n   217\t        hit = any(cyclic(r) for r in refs(figs[fid]))\n   218\t        state[fid] = 2\n   219\t        return hit\n   220\t    if any(cyclic(fid) for fid in figs):\n   221\t        errors.append(('C7', 'the figure graph has a cycle'))\n   222\t        return {'errors': errors, 'recorded': recorded}\n   223\t\n   224\t    # C1 sources, prior pointers\n   225\t    for fig in figs.values():\n   226\t        if fig['kind'] == 'source':\n   227\t            errors += _source_errors(fig, passages)\n   228\t        if fig['kind'] == 'prior' and not fig.get('pointer'):\n   229\t            errors.append(('C7', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: a prior forecast needs an exact pointer to an earlier answer shown in the request'))\n   230\t\n   231\t    # C2 arithmetic and bound propagation\n   232\t    for fig in figs.values():\n   233\t        if fig['kind'] != 'computed' or fig.get('operation') not in OPERATIONS:\n   234\t            continue\n   235\t        ins = [figs[i] for i in fig['inputs'] if i in figs]\n   236\t        expected = _compute(fig['operation'], [_interval(i) + (i['unit'],) for i in ins], fig.get('signs'), fig['unit'])\n   237\t        lo, hi = _interval(fig)\n   238\t        if fig['operation'] == 'range_from_relative' or ('low' in fig):\n   239\t            ok = _close(lo, expected[0], fig['unit']) and _close(hi, expected[1], fig['unit'])\n   240\t        else:\n   241\t            ok = _close(lo, (expected[0] + expected[1]) / 2, fig['unit'])\n   242\t        if not ok:\n   243\t            errors.append(('C2', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: declared {lo}–{hi} but {fig[\"operation\"]} of {fig[\"inputs\"]} gives {expected[0]:.2f}–{expected[1]:.2f}'))\n   244\t        want = _bound_direction(fig['operation'], ins)\n   245\t        have = DIRECTION.get(fig.get('bound'))\n   246\t        if want is not None and have != want:\n   247\t            errors.append(('C2', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: its inputs make it a {want} bound, but it is declared {fig.get(\"bound\") or \"a point\"}'))\n   248\t        elif want is None and fig.get('bound'):\n   249\t            errors.append(('C2', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: its inputs are points, but it is declared a bound ({fig[\"bound\"]})'))\n   250\t\n   251\t    # C8 operand compatibility\n   252\t    for fig in figs.values():\n   253\t        if fig['kind'] != 'computed' or fig.get('operation') not in OPERATIONS:\n   254\t            continue\n   255\t        ins = [figs[i] for i in fig['inputs'] if i in figs]\n   256\t        op, rel, out = fig['operation'], fig.get('relation'), fig['what']\n   257\t        differing = [i['id'] for i in ins if i['unit'] not in ('%', 'x') and\n   258\t                     (i['what']['population'], i['what']['scope'], i['what']['period'], i['what']['measure']) !=\n   259\t                     (out['population'], out['scope'], out['period'], out['measure'])]\n   260\t        if op in ('sum', 'difference'):\n   261\t            money = [i for i in ins if i['unit'] not in ('%', 'x')]\n   262\t            same_qty = all((i['what']['population'], i['what']['measure'], i['what']['scope']) ==\n   263\t                           (out['population'], out['measure'], out['scope']) for i in money)\n   264\t            if rel == 'time_aggregation':\n   265\t                qs = [_quarters(i['what']['period']) for i in money]\n   310\t    # answers: C7 coverage and ownership, C6 rung, C5 reference\n   311\t    members = family['members']\n   312\t    seen = {}\n   313\t    for ans in calc['answers']:\n   314\t        seen[ans['view_id']] = seen.get(ans['view_id'], 0) + 1\n   315\t    for view_id in members:\n   316\t        if seen.get(view_id, 0) != 1:\n   317\t            errors.append(('C7', f'{view_id} has {seen.get(view_id, 0)} answers; exactly one is required'))\n   318\t    for view_id in seen:\n   319\t        if view_id not in members:\n   320\t            errors.append(('C7', f'{view_id} is not a member of the family'))\n   321\t    outcomes = {}\n   322\t    for ans in calc['answers']:\n   323\t        member = members.get(ans['view_id'])\n   324\t        if member is None:\n   325\t            continue\n   326\t        if ans.get('shape') == 'unresolved':\n   327\t            if 'outcome' in ans or 'rung' in ans or not ans.get('why'):\n   328\t                errors.append(('C7', f'{ans[\"view_id\"]}: an unresolved answer has a reason and neither outcome nor rung'))\n   329\t            continue\n   330\t        out = figs.get(ans.get('outcome'))\n   331\t        if out is None:\n   332\t            errors.append(('C7', f'{ans[\"view_id\"]}: outcome {ans.get(\"outcome\")} is not a figure'))\n   333\t            continue\n   334\t        if _key(out['what']) != _key(member['what']):\n   335\t            errors.append(('C7', f'{ans[\"view_id\"]}: outcome {out[\"id\"]} measures {_key(out[\"what\"])}, not the question\\'s {_key(member[\"what\"])}'))\n   336\t        outcomes[ans['view_id']] = out['id']\n   337\t        lo, hi = _interval(out)\n   338\t        band = member['bands'][ans['rung'] - 1]\n   339\t        b_lo, b_hi = band[0] if band[0] is not None else float('-inf'), band[1] if band[1] is not None else float('inf')\n   340\t        if not (lo < b_hi and hi >= b_lo):\n   341\t            errors.append(('C6', f'{ans[\"view_id\"]}: rung {ans[\"rung\"]} ({band}) contains no part of its outcome {lo}–{hi}'))\n   342\t        ref = ans.get('reference') or {}\n   343\t        if ('figure' in ref) == ('unavailable' in ref):          # [46g.2] exactly one choice\n   344\t            errors.append(('C5', f'{ans[\"view_id\"]}: the reference must name exactly one of a figure or unavailable'))\n   345\t        elif 'unavailable' in ref:\n   346\t            if not ref['unavailable']:\n   347\t                errors.append(('C5', f'{ans[\"view_id\"]}: an unavailable reference needs a reason'))\n   348\t        else:\n   349\t            errors += _reference_errors(ans['view_id'], figs.get(ref.get('figure')), figs, passages, refs)\n   350\t\n   351\t    # [46i.1] a range summary is an estimate with low and high, is an answer's outcome, and no figure reads it\n   352\t    outcome_ids = {a.get('outcome') for a in calc['answers']}\n   353\t    for f in figs.values():\n   354\t        if f.get('scenario') != 'range':\n   355\t            continue\n   356\t        readers = [g['id'] for g in figs.values() if f['id'] in refs(g)]\n   357\t        if f['kind'] != 'estimate' or 'low' not in f or 'high' not in f or f['id'] not in outcome_ids or readers:\n   358\t            errors.append(('C4', f'{f[\"id\"]}: a range summary must be an estimate with low and high that is an answer\\'s outcome and feeds no figure'\n   359\t                                 + (f' (read by {\", \".join(readers)})' if readers else '')))\n   360\t\n   361\t    # C3 part within whole, C4 one forecast per shared quantity (every path)\n   362\t    def reachable(start, stop=None):\n   363\t        stops = set(stop) if isinstance(stop, (set, list, tuple)) else {stop}\n   364\t        seen_ids, stack = set(), [start]\n   365\t        while stack:\n   366\t            fid = stack.pop()\n   367\t            if fid in seen_ids or fid not in figs:\n   368\t                continue\n   369\t            seen_ids.add(fid)\n   370\t            if fid not in stops:\n   371\t                stack.extend(refs(figs[fid]))\n   372\t        return seen_ids\n   373\t    scenarios = {f.get('scenario', 'base') for f in figs.values() if f['basis'] == 'forecast'} or {'base'}\n   374\t    for rel in family.get('relations', []):\n   375\t        if rel['type'] != 'part_of' or rel['part'] not in outcomes or rel['whole'] not in outcomes:\n   376\t            continue\n   377\t        part_m, whole_m = members[rel['part']], members[rel['whole']]\n   378\t        for sc in scenarios:\n   379\t            for period in family.get('compare_periods', []):\n   380\t                def node(view_id, member):\n   381\t                    want = (member['what']['population'], member['what']['measure'], member['what']['scope'], period)\n   382\t                    hits = [figs[f] for f in reachable(outcomes[view_id]) if _key(figs[f]['what']) == want\n   383\t                            and figs[f]['basis'] == 'forecast' and figs[f].get('scenario', 'base') == sc]\n   384\t                    return hits[0] if hits else None\n   385\t                p, w = node(rel['part'], part_m), node(rel['whole'], whole_m)\n   386\t                if p and w:\n   387\t                    (plo, phi), (wlo, whi) = _interval(p), _interval(w)\n   388\t                    if plo > wlo + 1e-9 or phi > whi + 1e-9:\n   389\t                        errors.append(('C3', f'{period} {sc}: {rel[\"part\"]} {p[\"id\"]} ({plo}–{phi}) exceeds {rel[\"whole\"]} {w[\"id\"]} ({wlo}–{whi})'))\n   390\t    for shared in family.get('shared', []):\n   391\t        want = _key(shared)\n   392\t        nodes = [f for f in figs.values() if _key(f['what']) == want and f['basis'] == 'forecast']\n   393\t        touched = [v for v, o in outcomes.items() if any(_key(figs[f]['what']) == want for f in reachable(o))]\n   394\t        if not touched:\n   395\t            continue\n   396\t        per_scenario = {}\n   397\t        for n in nodes:\n   398\t            per_scenario.setdefault(n.get('scenario', 'base'), []).append(n['id'])\n   399\t        if not nodes:\n   400\t            errors.append(('C4', f'{want}: no forecast node, though {\", \".join(touched)} depend on it'))\n   401\t        for sc, ids in sorted(per_scenario.items()):\n   402\t            if len(ids) != 1:\n   403\t                errors.append(('C4', f'{want} {sc}: {len(ids)} forecast nodes ({\", \".join(ids)}); exactly one per scenario is required'))\n   404\t        stop = {n['id'] for n in nodes}\n   405\t        for f in figs.values():                       # [46i.1] scenario membership is derived along the whole path, not declared\n   406\t            sc = f.get('scenario', 'base')\n   407\t            if sc == 'range' or f['kind'] not in ('computed', 'estimate'):\n   408\t                continue\n   409\t            upstream = _upstream_of(f['id'], figs, refs)\n   410\t            borrowed = sorted(r for r in upstream if r in stop and figs[r].get('scenario', 'base') != sc)\n   411\t            if borrowed:\n   412\t                errors.append(('C4', f'{want}: {f[\"id\"]} ({sc}) depends on {\", \".join(borrowed)} of another scenario'))\n   413\t        for view_id in touched:                      # [46g.3] a bypass reaches the quantity through no forecast node of any scenario\n   414\t            bypass = [f for f in reachable(outcomes[view_id], stop=stop) if f not in stop and _key(figs[f]['what']) == want]\n   415\t            if bypass:\n   416\t                errors.append(('C4', f'{want}: {view_id} reaches {\", \".join(sorted(bypass))} without passing a forecast node ({\", \".join(sorted(stop))})'))\n   417\t    for rel in family.get('relations', []):\n   418\t        if rel['type'] != 'same_base' or rel['later'] not in outcomes or rel['earlier'] not in outcomes:\n   419\t            continue\n   420\t        base_id, base_key = outcomes[rel['earlier']], _key(members[rel['earlier']]['what'])\n   421\t        reached = reachable(outcomes[rel['later']], stop=base_id)\n   422\t        bypass = [f for f in reached if f != base_id and _key(figs[f]['what']) == base_key]\n   423\t        if base_id not in reached:\n   424\t            errors.append(('C9', f'{rel[\"later\"]} does not rest on {rel[\"earlier\"]}\\'s forecast {base_id}'))\n   425\t        if bypass:\n   426\t            errors.append(('C9', f'{rel[\"later\"]} reaches {\", \".join(sorted(bypass))} for {base_key} without {rel[\"earlier\"]}\\'s forecast {base_id}'))\n   427\t    supplied = family.get('prior_answers', {})\n   428\t    for fig in figs.values():\n   429\t        earlier = fig['kind'] == 'prior' or fig.get('basis') == 'prior_forecast' or 'pointer' in fig   # [46i.2] derived, not labelled\n   430\t        if not earlier:\n   431\t            continue\n   432\t        if fig['kind'] != 'prior' or fig.get('basis') != 'prior_forecast':\n   433\t            errors.append(('C10', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: an earlier forecast must be kind prior with basis prior_forecast'))\n   434\t        ptr, ans_prior = fig.get('pointer', {}), supplied.get(fig.get('pointer', {}).get('view'), {})\n   435\t        if ans_prior.get('day') != ptr.get('day') or not any(_same(fig.get('value'), v) for v in ans_prior.get('values', [])):\n   436\t            errors.append(('C10', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: no earlier answer of {ptr.get(\"view\")} on {ptr.get(\"day\")} shown in the request states {fig.get(\"value\")}'))\n   437\t        owners = [a['view_id'] for a in calc['answers'] if a.get('outcome') == fig['id']]\n   438\t        if owners:                                    # [46h.2] nor the current outcome\n   439\t            errors.append(('C10', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: an earlier forecast cannot be the current outcome of {\", \".join(owners)}'))\n   440\t        users = [f['id'] for f in figs.values() if fig['id'] in refs(f)]\n   441\t        if users:\n   442\t            errors.append(('C10', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: an earlier forecast is for comparison only and cannot feed {\", \".join(users)}'))\n   443\t\n   444\t    recorded += _assumptions(family, figs, outcomes, calc, refs)\n   445\t    return {'errors': errors, 'recorded': recorded}\n   446\t\n   447\t\n   448\tdef _per_unit(op, ins, fig):\n   449\t    \"\"\"The per-unit identity: ratio(total, price per unit) -> units, product(units, price per unit) -> total, for one population and\n   450\t    scope. Labels are the judge's; a reader checks them against the passages.\"\"\"\n   451\t    out = fig['what']\n   452\t    if len(ins) != 2:\n   453\t        return False\n   454\t    same = all((i['what']['population'], i['what']['scope']) == (out['population'], out['scope']) for i in ins)\n   455\t    price = [i for i in ins if i['what']['measure'] == 'price per unit' and i['unit'] in ('USD', 'USD bn')]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba DESIGN.md | sed -n '28,65p;147,180p'; cat REQUEST-AUDIT.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba gate.py | sed -n '20,140p;215,249p;306,375p'; rg -n 'converts|disputed|_upstream_of|def _assumptions' calc_check.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba DESIGN.md | sed -n '28,65p;147,180p'; cat REQUEST-AUDIT.md\"","aggregated_output":"    28\t\n    29\t```\n    30\tfigures: [ { id,\n    31\t             what: { population, measure, scope, period },     # canonical: measure is the quantity (\"revenue\"), not its basis [46.1]\n    32\t             basis: \"reported\" | \"guidance\" | \"consensus\" | \"third_party\" | \"forecast\" | \"prior_forecast\",\n    33\t             scenario: \"base\" | \"<named>\",                       # default \"base\" [46.1]\n    34\t             kind: \"source\" | \"computed\" | \"estimate\",\n    35\t             value | {low, high} | {bound: \">\" | \">=\" | \"<\" | \"<=\" | \"approx\" | \"approx_below\" | \"approx_above\", value} | {multiplier, bound?},  unit,   # [46c.3]\n    36\t             # kind source:   evidence: \"<id>\", expression: <index of a complete expression code extracts from that passage>,\n    37\t             #                component: \"midpoint\" | \"low\" | \"high\" | \"bound\" | \"multiplier\" | \"value\"            [46b.2]\n    38\t             # kind computed: inputs: [...], operation: sum|difference|product|ratio|growth|apply_growth|share|range_from_relative|roll_forward,   # [46c.2]\n    39\t             #                relation (sum and roll_forward): \"accounting_parts\" | \"time_aggregation\" | \"stated_in_addition\" | \"overlap_unknown\",\n    40\t             #                disputed (overlap_unknown only): \"<the operand whose inclusion is in doubt>\"            [46b.4, 46d]\n    41\t             #                bridge (when inputs' what differ from the output's): \"<figure id of an estimate>\"   [46.3]\n    42\t             # kind estimate: basis_text, rests_on: [figure ids, evidence ids],\n    43\t             #                adjusts (optional): { figure: \"<id>\", type: \"discount\" | \"uplift\" | \"trim\" }            [46.3]\n    44\t             #                a bridge estimate also names `converts: [operand ids]` and the assumption           [46b.3]\n    45\t           } ]\n    46\tanswers: [ { view_id, shape: \"forecast\", outcome: \"<figure id>\", rung,                 # [46b.5] two shapes\n    47\t             reference: { figure: \"<id>\" } | { unavailable: \"<why>\" },                # per answer [46.2]\n    48\t             reasons, cites, pushes, theme_pushes, changed, why_changed }\n    49\t         | { view_id, shape: \"unresolved\", why, cites, changed, why_changed } ]       # no outcome, no rung\n    50\t```\n    51\t\n    52\t- **An arithmetic intermediate and the analyst's final range are distinct figures** [46.2]. For example, q02's $392B × 92% is a\n    53\t  `computed` figure. The final $370–400B is an `estimate` resting on it and on q01's range. Code checks the intermediate's arithmetic\n    54\t  and never requires the final range to equal it.\n    55\t- **`prior`** figures (basis `prior_forecast`) are for comparison only [46f.4]. They need a pointer to an earlier answer shown in the\n    56\t  request and must equal a figure that answer states (C10). They may feed no figure. A declared `same_base` reads the family's own\n    57\t  forecast node of the earlier member at the same snapshot (q22 reads q01's): C9.\n    58\t- **`roll_forward`** [46c.2]: an opening balance as of a date, plus additions and minus drawdowns over a later period, gives the\n    59\t  balance at that period's end. It is the accounting identity for a stock and its flows. An addition whose inclusion in the opening\n    60\t  balance is in doubt carries `relation: overlap_unknown` and `disputed` (R2's $18B).\n    61\t- **Scenarios carry ranges** [46b.1]. A forecast node is a point within a scenario. A range across members is written as paired\n    62\t  scenarios (for example `low`, `high`) whose nodes stay paired. The analyst's final answer may be a range `estimate` resting on the\n    63\t  scenario outcomes.\n    64\t- **The family declaration** (by the harness, not by the answer) lists the shared quantities and periods the members depend on, for\n    65\t  example company revenue for each FY2027 quarter, and the typed relations [46b.1].\n   147\t- **Added:** how to write figures (kinds, bases, expressions, relations, bridges, `adjusts`, `unresolved`).\n   148\t- **The audit:** every changed sentence is shown with its source (D260, D263, D725, this design), read against a stored family\n   149\t  request, and its character count before and after is reported (AGENTS §6).\n   150\t\n   151\t## 6. The $0 gate (registered; each defect must produce its named finding) [46.5]\n   152\t\n   153\t| Item | Content | Pass: the named finding |\n   154\t|---|---|---|\n   155\t| R1a | old-2 8729 (v14) and 8737 (v9) on 09-20, as stored: v9 Q4 146, v14 Q4 127 | **C3** on Q4 |\n   156\t| R1b | the same, with Q3 as stored: **one** guide node (midpoint 108 from e2499, labelled `guidance`) feeds v14's company Q3 forecast (113.5, beat-adjusted) and, on a second path, v9's Data Center Q3 (108 × 92.5% = 99.9) | **C4** on Q3 company revenue (the bypass path), independent of C3 |\n   157\t| R1c (control) | the same guide node (midpoint 108 ±2%, e2499's expression) feeding one shared Q3 forecast node (113.5) that both members read | passes |\n   158\t| R2 | old-2 8734 as `roll_forward`: the $25B balance as of July 26 (e2620), plus the $18B committed for the rest of the fiscal year (e2889) as `overlap_unknown` and `disputed`, plus MediaTek and the talks as estimates | passes C8; recorded overlap; the alternate without the $18B (about $35B) decides the $50B boundary (conditional) |\n   159\t| R3 | old-2 8595: 730 (e1786, bound \">\") / 800 (e2535, bound \"approx_below\") × 1,300 (e2535, point) | stripped qualifiers: **C1**. Qualifiers kept: passes C1, then **C8** without a bridge naming those operands. With the bridge: recorded, undetermined |\n   160\t| R4 | old-3 9166: 20 × (>2) (e3660, \"more than double\") gives >40, trimmed to 38–39 by `adjusts: trim` | recorded adjustment that definitely crosses the $40B boundary (rung 2 is $40–50B, rung 1 $50B+) |\n   161\t| G1–G4 (controls) | q01, q02, q19, q22, from `gold-v1.json`'s reasoning (expressions from the packet items). q01's Q1 + Q2 as `time_aggregation`; q02's comparison $392B (consensus) × 92% (reported mix); q22 in one family with q01, reading q01's FY2027 node | all pass, estimates visible; q02's reference passes C5; q19's overlapping range passes C6 with its reason |\n   162\t| P1–P3 (plants, on control copies) | P1, an amount absent from its expression; P2, a wrong sum; P3a, a prior forecast as the reference; P3b, the same figure wrapped in an estimate that cites outside evidence | P1 **C1**, P2 **C2**, P3a and P3b **C5**, each for its intended reason |\n   163\t| T1–T7 (C1 forms, real passages) | e2499 midpoint 108 ±2% (accepted as `midpoint`); e1786 \">730\"; e2535 approx_below 800 and the point 1,300; e3660 \">×2\"; stripped forms \"$730\", \"800\", \"double\" against those passages; 108.5 against e2499 | T1–T3 parse as stated; the stripped forms and 108.5 refused |\n   164\t| U1–U2 (paths) | a member answering `unresolved` while another member's outcome needs its shared quantity; a calculation refused twice | the family held, recorded; the family unresolved, recorded |\n   165\t\n   166\t- **Stop:** any missing finding, a finding for the wrong reason, or a control the format cannot express.\n   167\t- **Then:** Council B on the gate's output. The paid gate's ceiling goes to Alex.\n# judging-v13 request audit (DESIGN.md §5; $0)\n\nThe system text is `judging-v13-draft.txt`: 4,835 characters, against judging-v7's 4,924 (−89). The format definitions sit in the schema\ndescriptions beside their fields (AGENTS §3, §6), not in the system text.\n\n## The system text, sentence by sentence against judging-v7\n\n| v7 sentence | v13 | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| L1 \"judging a thesis's current rung … Use only the supplied evidence, dependency conclusions and themes\" | \"the current rungs of a family of related number theses …\"; dependency conclusions removed | D725 (the unit is a family); the family has no dependency reads |\n| L3 \"the current conclusions of dependencies\" | removed | the same |\n| L3 \"Pieces in force … are not shown; the previous conclusion carries them\" | \"each member's earlier forecast reflects them, but its figures are our own, never a source and never the market's expectation\" | D198 kept; the self-made reference (D693 trace, `self-reference/RESULT.md`); C5 |\n| L3 \"Do not add to or subtract from the previous score. The previous conclusion is supplied only for comparison.\" | kept, per member | D260 |\n| L4 reference, run-rate, shifts, product-target discount | kept word for word, per member | D260, D263 (the frozen gold's reasoning) |\n| L4 \"State the implied figure or date, check it against the dependencies' conclusions shown (a part cannot exceed its whole, and a figure that spans several periods or products gives this question only its share)\" | \"Build the family's figures once and read every member's outcome from them: a part cannot exceed its whole, a figure that spans several periods or products gives a question only its share, and a quantity the family shares has one forecast per scenario\" | D260 clause (3), made family-wide; C3, C4 |\n| L5 tiers, novelty, discounting, sizing, identities | kept word for word | D260, D263 |\n| L6 replacement | kept | D198 |\n| L7 themes | kept, per member | D191, D195 |\n| L8 dependencies \"not yet created\" or \"historical only\" | removed | a family has no dependency reads (`cites_views` always empty) |\n| L9 consistency with dependencies and themes; \"a component cannot exceed its whole\" | \"consistent with each other and with the themes in force\"; the component clause moved into L4's family sentence | D260; the duplicate removed (AGENTS §6) |\n| L10 the output list (one rung, reference, implied_outcome …) | \"Return the family's figures and one answer per member, as the JSON schema defines them. Every number an answer rests on is a figure; a number you judge … is an estimate, stated as yours. When the evidence cannot support a member's forecast, answer it unresolved …\" | D725, DESIGN §2; field definitions moved to the schema |\n| L11 changed | kept | PRD 06 |\n\n**Read in both directions** (AGENTS §6):\n- No v13 sentence keeps wider or narrower than v7 on the standard.\n- The only new rules are the three D725 contracts: one calculation, figures labelled, and unresolved allowed. Code enforces each.\n- The product-target sentence (\"discounted by default\") is kept. D721 and Codex's round 43 found that the gold relies on it (q19).\n\n## The schema descriptions (the format's definitions, beside their fields)\n\n- **`figures[].what`:** \"What the number measures: population, measure (the quantity, such as revenue; never its basis), scope, period.\"\n- **`figures[].basis`:**\n  - reported: an actual;\n  - guidance: the company's outlook;\n  - consensus: analysts' average;\n  - third_party: one outside party;\n  - forecast: this family's forecast;\n  - prior_forecast: our earlier forecast, with its pointer.\n- **`figures[].kind`:**\n  - source: stated in a shown passage;\n  - computed: one operation on named figures;\n  - estimate: your judgement.\n- **`figures[].expression`, source only:** \"the complete numeric expression exactly as the passage writes it, qualifiers included (for\n  example 'more than $2 billion', '$4.5 billion, plus or minus 3%', 'more than triple')\". The examples come from no gate case [46f.4].\n- **`figures[].relation`, sum and roll_forward:**\n  - time_aggregation: periods of one quantity;\n  - accounting_parts: declared parts of a whole;\n  - stated_in_addition: a source says the amounts add;\n  - overlap_unknown: name the disputed figure.\n- **`figures[].bridge`:** \"Only when no listed identity covers the operation (periods of one quantity, declared parts, a balance and its\n  flows, a stated share or multiplier, a total over a per-unit price): an estimate stating the conversion and listing the operands it\n  converts.\" This matches C8's operation-specific rules, so q01's quarters-to-half and q02's mix applied to consensus need none [46f.4].\n- **`figures[].adjusts`, estimate only:** \"The stated figure this estimate changes, and how: discount, uplift or trim.\"\n- **`answers[]`:**\n  - **forecast:** the outcome figure, and the rung whose band contains it or, for a range spanning several bands, the band you choose,\n    with the reason. The reference is an external figure, or a calculation from external and reported figures, or `unavailable` with\n    why. It is never our earlier forecast.\n  - **unresolved:** why.\n\n## The family header (user message, before the evidence)\n\n`[Family] members: <id> (<question>, ladder …) …`, then:\n- `Relations: <part> is part of <whole>; <later> rests on <earlier>'s base.`\n- `Shared quantities, one forecast each per scenario: <population, measure, scope, period> …`\n\nThe family header, the members' earlier forecasts (labelled \"our earlier forecast, not a source\") and the union of evidence in view\nfollow the order of v7's request.\n\n## Earlier forecasts [46f.4]\n\nThe draft says the earlier forecasts are \"supplied only for comparison\", and C10 makes that a check: a `prior` figure feeds no figure.\nThe design's earlier clause allowing a dated prior to feed a `same_base` is withdrawn. A later year reads the earlier member's forecast\nnode in the same call (C9).\n\n## Rendered and checked (`render_v13.py`, `render-r1.*`)\n\n- **The request:** the old-2 family on 09-20 (calls 8729 and 8737). System text 4,835 characters; user message 123,304 characters, with\n  237 evidence items, the family header, the themes once and the earlier forecasts labelled; schema 10,066 characters.\n- **The answer:** the R1c control answer, in strict shape (every optional field null). It passes `model.check_schema` with no error and\n  calc_check with no error. Every passage it cites is in the rendered request.\n- **Tokens:** not counted here. The two v7 calls were 36,151 input tokens together (Codex, round 45b).\n\n## Not yet done\n\n- The product request builder (the harness renderer above is not it).\n- The sender for the paid gate.\n\nBoth are build work after the $0 gate.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba gate.py | sed -n '20,140p;215,249p;306,375p'; rg -n 'converts|disputed|_upstream_of|def _assumptions' calc_check.py\"","aggregated_output":"    20\t    rows = conn.execute(f'select evidence_id, quote, speaker from evidence where evidence_id in ({\",\".join(\"?\" * len(ids))})', ids).fetchall()\n    21\t    assert len(rows) == len(ids), (draw, ids, rows)\n    22\t    return {e: {'text': q, 'speaker': s} for e, q, s in rows}\n    23\t\n    24\t\n    25\tdef packet_passages(ids):\n    26\t    items = {it['id']: it for it in json.loads(PACKET.read_text())['items']}\n    27\t    return {i: {'text': items[i]['passage'], 'speaker': items[i]['who']} for i in ids}\n    28\t\n    29\t\n    30\tdef W(population, measure, scope, period):\n    31\t    return {'population': population, 'measure': measure, 'scope': scope, 'period': period}\n    32\t\n    33\t\n    34\tdef src(fid, evidence, expression, value, unit, basis, what, component='value', bound=None):\n    35\t    fig = {'id': fid, 'kind': 'source', 'evidence': evidence, 'expression': expression, 'component': component, 'value': value,\n    36\t           'unit': unit, 'basis': basis, 'what': what}\n    37\t    if bound:\n    38\t        fig['bound'] = bound\n    39\t    return fig\n    40\t\n    41\t\n    42\tdef comp(fid, op, inputs, value, unit, what, basis='forecast', **extra):\n    43\t    fig = {'id': fid, 'kind': 'computed', 'operation': op, 'inputs': inputs, 'unit': unit, 'basis': basis, 'what': what}\n    44\t    fig.update({'low': value[0], 'high': value[1]} if isinstance(value, tuple) else {'value': value})\n    45\t    fig.update(extra)\n    46\t    return fig\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\tdef est(fid, value, unit, what, basis_text, rests_on=(), basis='forecast', **extra):\n    50\t    fig = {'id': fid, 'kind': 'estimate', 'unit': unit, 'basis': basis, 'what': what, 'basis_text': basis_text, 'rests_on': list(rests_on)}\n    51\t    fig.update({'low': value[0], 'high': value[1]} if isinstance(value, tuple) else {'value': value})\n    52\t    fig.update(extra)\n    53\t    return fig\n    54\t\n    55\t\n    56\tdef ans(view_id, outcome, rung, reference):\n    57\t    return {'view_id': view_id, 'shape': 'forecast', 'outcome': outcome, 'rung': rung, 'reference': reference, 'reasons': 'r', 'cites': [],\n    58\t            'pushes': [], 'theme_pushes': [], 'changed': True, 'why_changed': 'w'}\n    59\t\n    60\t\n    61\t# ---------- R1: old-2 calls 8729 (v14) and 8737 (v9), 2026-09-20 ----------\n    62\tBANDS_OLD2_REV = [[450, None], [400, 450], [350, 400], [300, 350], [None, 300]]\n    63\tCO, DC = 'company', 'Data Center'\n    64\tR1_FAMILY = {'members': {'v14': {'what': W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027'), 'bands': BANDS_OLD2_REV},\n    65\t                         'v9': {'what': W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027'), 'bands': BANDS_OLD2_REV}},\n    66\t             'relations': [{'type': 'part_of', 'part': 'v9', 'whole': 'v14'}],\n    67\t             'shared': [W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 Q3'), W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 Q4')],\n    68\t             'compare_periods': ['FY2027 Q3', 'FY2027 Q4', 'FY2027'],\n    69\t             'prior_answers': {'v9': {'day': '2026-09-19', 'values': [414.0, 385.0, 390.0]}}}   # call 8621: reference $414B, outcome $385–390B\n    70\tR1_PASSAGES = store_passages('old-2', ['e238', 'e2497', 'e2499', 'e4762', 'e3943', 'e5056', 'e4995', 'e3219', 'e976'])\n    71\t\n    72\t\n    73\tdef r1_common():\n    74\t    return [\n    75\t        src('q1', 'e238', '$81.6 billion', 81.6, 'USD bn', 'reported', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 Q1')),\n    76\t        src('q2', 'e2497', '$96.2 billion', 96.2, 'USD bn', 'reported', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 Q2')),\n    77\t        src('g3', 'e2499', '$108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%', 108.0, 'USD bn', 'guidance', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 Q3'), 'midpoint'),\n    78\t        src('g3w', 'e2499', '$108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%', 2.0, '%', 'guidance', W('NVIDIA', 'guidance width', CO, 'FY2027 Q3'), 'relative'),\n    79\t        comp('g3r', 'range_from_relative', ['g3', 'g3w'], (105.84, 110.16), 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 Q3'), basis='guidance'),\n    80\t        src('beat', 'e4762', '3.1%', 3.1, '%', 'third_party', W('NVIDIA', 'beat over the guidance high end', CO, 'last four quarters')),\n    81\t        est('q3f', 113.5, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 Q3'), 'the guide high end 110.16 plus the 3.1% average beat', ['g3r', 'beat']),\n    82\t        src('g12', 'e3943', '12%', 12.0, '%', 'third_party', W('NVIDIA', 'sequential growth', CO, 'FY2027 Q3')),\n    83\t        est('carry', 12.0, '%', W('NVIDIA', 'assumption', CO, 'FY2027 Q4'), \"Q3's guided 12% sequential growth continues into Q4\", ['g12'],\n    84\t            converts=['q3f']),\n    85\t        comp('q4f', 'apply_growth', ['q3f', 'g12'], 127.1, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 Q4'), bridge='carry'),\n    86\t        comp('fy14', 'sum', ['q1', 'q2', 'q3f', 'q4f'], 418.4, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027'), relation='time_aggregation'),\n    87\t        src('c411', 'e5056', 'around $411 billion', 411.0, 'USD bn', 'consensus', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027'), 'bound', 'approx'),\n    88\t        src('dch1', 'e4995', '$164 billion', 164.0, 'USD bn', 'reported', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027 H1')),\n    89\t        src('mix', 'e3219', '92.5%', 92.5, '%', 'reported', W('NVIDIA', 'Data Center share', CO, 'FY2027 Q2')),\n    90\t    ]\n    91\t\n    92\t\n    93\tdef r1(variant):\n    94\t    figs = r1_common()\n    95\t    if variant in ('a', 'b'):\n    96\t        figs.append(comp('dcq3', 'share', ['g3', 'mix'], 99.9, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027 Q3')))\n    97\t    else:\n    98\t        figs.append(comp('dcq3', 'share', ['q3f', 'mix'], 105.0, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027 Q3')))\n    99\t    if variant == 'a':\n   100\t        figs.append(est('dcq4', 146.0, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027 Q4'),\n   101\t                        'hyperscale reacceleration, the Rubin ramp, a discounted SemiAnalysis uplift', ['e976']))\n   102\t        dcfy = 409.9\n   103\t    elif variant == 'b':\n   104\t        figs.append(est('dcq4', 115.0, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027 Q4'), 'held below the company quarter', ['e976']))\n   105\t        dcfy = 378.9\n   106\t    else:\n   107\t        figs.append(comp('dcq4', 'share', ['q4f', 'mix'], 117.6, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027 Q4')))\n   108\t        dcfy = 386.6\n   109\t    figs.append(comp('dcfy', 'sum', ['dch1', 'dcq3', 'dcq4'], dcfy, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027'), relation='time_aggregation'))\n   110\t    if variant == 'a':                                    # as stored: the previous conclusion's $414B called the market reference\n   111\t        figs.append({'id': 'prior414', 'kind': 'prior', 'basis': 'prior_forecast', 'value': 414.0, 'unit': 'USD bn',\n   112\t                     'what': W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027'), 'pointer': {'view': 'v9', 'day': '2026-09-19'}})   # its reference field, $414B since 09-14 (call 7939)\n   113\t        v9_ref = {'figure': 'prior414'}\n   114\t    else:\n   115\t        figs.append(comp('dcref', 'share', ['c411', 'mix'], 380.2, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027'), basis='consensus', bound='approx'))\n   116\t        v9_ref = {'figure': 'dcref'}\n   117\t    v9_rung = 2 if dcfy >= 400 else 3\n   118\t    return {'figures': figs, 'answers': [ans('v14', 'fy14', 2, {'figure': 'c411'}), ans('v9', 'dcfy', v9_rung, v9_ref)]}\n   119\t\n   120\t\n   121\t# ---------- R2: old-2 call 8734 (v29 equity commitments) ----------\n   122\tR2_FAMILY = {'members': {'v29': {'what': W('NVIDIA', 'equity investment commitments', CO, 'end of FY2027'),\n   123\t                                 'bands': [[None, 25], [25, 50], [50, 75], [75, 100], [100, None]]}},\n   124\t             'relations': [], 'shared': [], 'compare_periods': []}\n   125\tR2_PASSAGES = store_passages('old-2', ['e2620', 'e2889', 'e1732'])\n   126\t\n   127\t\n   128\tdef r2():\n   129\t    eic = 'equity investment commitments'\n   130\t    return {'figures': [\n   131\t        src('bal', 'e2620', '$25 billion', 25.0, 'USD bn', 'reported', W('NVIDIA', eic, CO, 'as of 2026-07-26')),\n   132\t        src('add18', 'e2889', '$18 billion', 18.0, 'USD bn', 'reported', W('NVIDIA', eic, CO, 'rest of FY2027')),\n   133\t        est('mtk', 3.5, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', eic, CO, 'rest of FY2027'), 'the MediaTek investment announced after the balance date'),\n   134\t        est('talks', 6.5, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', eic, CO, 'rest of FY2027'), 'the Anthropic and Thinking Machines talks, risk-adjusted (amount inferred from the stated $53B total)'),\n   135\t        src('ref70', 'e1732', '$70 billion', 70.0, 'USD bn', 'third_party', W('NVIDIA', 'equity investments to ecosystem partners', CO, 'period not specified')),\n   136\t        comp('end', 'roll_forward', ['bal', 'add18', 'mtk', 'talks'], 53.0, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', eic, CO, 'end of FY2027'),\n   137\t             relation='overlap_unknown', disputed='add18'),\n   138\t    ], 'answers': [ans('v29', 'end', 3, {'figure': 'ref70'})]}                     # as stored: Bank of America's $70B\n   139\t\n   140\t\n   215\t\n   216\t\n   217\tdef g1():\n   218\t    return ({'members': {'v1': V1}, 'relations': [], 'shared': [], 'compare_periods': []},\n   219\t            {'figures': q01_figs(), 'answers': [ans('v1', 'gfy', 2, {'figure': 'gc392'})]})\n   220\t\n   221\t\n   222\tdef g2():\n   223\t    \"\"\"q01 and q02 with paired scenarios [46g.3]: low and high paths for the company total and the segment, each final range an estimate.\"\"\"\n   224\t    figs = [f for f in q01_figs() if f['id'] in ('gq1', 'gq2', 'gh1', 'gc392')] + [\n   225\t        est('gh2lo', 228.0, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 H2'), 'the low end of the second-half drivers',\n   226\t            ['i295', 'i106', 'i219', 'i216', 'i288'], scenario='low'),\n   227\t        est('gh2hi', 262.0, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 H2'), 'the high end of the second-half drivers',\n   228\t            ['i295', 'i106', 'i219', 'i216', 'i288'], scenario='high'),\n   229\t        comp('gfylo', 'sum', ['gh1', 'gh2lo'], 400.6, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027'), relation='time_aggregation', scenario='low'),\n   230\t        comp('gfyhi', 'sum', ['gh1', 'gh2hi'], 434.6, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027'), relation='time_aggregation', scenario='high'),\n   231\t        est('gfy', (400.0, 435.0), 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027'), 'the two paths, rounded', ['gfylo', 'gfyhi'], scenario='range'),\n   232\t        src('gmix', 'i129', '92%', 92.0, '%', 'reported', W('NVIDIA', 'Data Center share', CO, 'FY2027 Q1')),\n   233\t        comp('gref2', 'share', ['gc392', 'gmix'], 360.6, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027'), basis='consensus'),\n   234\t        est('gshlo', 92.0, '%', W('NVIDIA', 'Data Center share', CO, 'FY2027'), 'the Q1 mix, held', ['gmix'], scenario='low'),\n   235\t        est('gshhi', 93.0, '%', W('NVIDIA', 'Data Center share', CO, 'FY2027'), 'the Q1 mix, a point higher', ['gmix'], scenario='high'),\n   236\t        comp('gdclo', 'share', ['gfylo', 'gshlo'], 368.55, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027'), scenario='low'),\n   237\t        comp('gdchi', 'share', ['gfyhi', 'gshhi'], 404.18, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027'), scenario='high'),\n   238\t        est('gdc', (370.0, 400.0), 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027'), 'the two paths, with the compute tracking',\n   239\t            ['gdclo', 'gdchi', 'i106'], scenario='range'),\n   240\t    ]\n   241\t    family = {'members': {'v1': V1, 'v2': {'what': W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027'), 'bands': SEED['v2']}},\n   242\t              'relations': [{'type': 'part_of', 'part': 'v2', 'whole': 'v1'}],\n   243\t              'shared': [W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027')], 'compare_periods': ['FY2027']}\n   244\t    return family, {'figures': figs, 'answers': [ans('v1', 'gfy', 2, {'figure': 'gc392'}), ans('v2', 'gdc', 2, {'figure': 'gref2'})]}\n   245\t\n   246\t\n   247\tdef g3():\n   248\t    figs = [\n   249\t        src('gt20', 'i288', '$20 billion', 20.0, 'USD bn', 'guidance', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', 'Vera CPU', 'FY2027')),\n   306\t         lambda r: (not r['errors'] and sum(x['type'] == 'bridge' for x in r['recorded']) == 2, 'bridges recorded, undetermined'), '')\n   307\t    item('R4', R4_FAMILY, R4_PASSAGES, r4(),\n   308\t         lambda r: (not r['errors'] and any(x['type'] == 'adjustment' and x['figure'] == 'vera28' and 40 in x['boundaries_crossed']\n   309\t                                            and x['certainty'] == 'definite' for x in r['recorded']), 'trim definitely crosses 40'), '')\n   310\t    for name, maker in (('G1', g1), ('G2', g2), ('G3', g3), ('G4', g4)):\n   311\t        family, calc = maker()\n   312\t        item(name, family, G_PASSAGES, calc, lambda r: (not r['errors'], 'passes, estimates visible'), '')\n   313\t    f1, c1 = g1()\n   314\t    p1 = copy.deepcopy(c1)\n   315\t    p1['figures'][0]['value'] = 81.9\n   316\t    item('P1', f1, G_PASSAGES, p1, lambda r: (codes(r) == {'C1'} and any('gq1' in d for _, d in r['errors']), 'C1 only, on gq1'), '')\n   317\t    p2 = copy.deepcopy(c1)\n   318\t    gfy = next(f for f in p2['figures'] if f['id'] == 'gfy')\n   319\t    gfy['low'], gfy['high'] = 450.0, 480.0\n   320\t    item('P2', f1, G_PASSAGES, p2, lambda r: (codes(r) == {'C2'} and any('gfy' in d for _, d in r['errors']), 'C2 only, on gfy'), '')\n   321\t    p3a = copy.deepcopy(c1)\n   322\t    p3a['figures'].append({'id': 'pri', 'kind': 'prior', 'basis': 'prior_forecast', 'value': 425.0, 'unit': 'USD bn',\n   323\t                           'what': W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027'), 'pointer': {'view': 'v1', 'day': '2026-07-13'}})\n   324\t    p3a['answers'][0]['reference'] = {'figure': 'pri'}\n   325\t    f1p = dict(f1, prior_answers={'v1': {'day': '2026-07-13', 'values': [425.0]}})       # the earlier answer it points to, as shown\n   326\t    item('P3a', f1p, G_PASSAGES, p3a, lambda r: (codes(r) == {'C5'}, 'C5 only'), '')\n   327\t    f2, c2 = g2()\n   328\t    g2x = copy.deepcopy(c2)\n   329\t    lo = next(f for f in g2x['figures'] if f['id'] == 'gdclo'); hi = next(f for f in g2x['figures'] if f['id'] == 'gdchi')\n   330\t    lo['inputs'], lo['value'] = ['gfyhi', 'gshlo'], 399.83                  # crossed: low share on the high total\n   331\t    hi['inputs'], hi['value'] = ['gfylo', 'gshhi'], 372.56\n   332\t    item('G2x', f2, G_PASSAGES, g2x, lambda r: (any(c == 'C4' and 'another scenario' in d for c, d in r['errors']), 'C4: scenarios crossed'), '')\n   333\t    r1x = r1('b')\n   334\t    r1x['figures'].append(est('altq3', 108.0, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 Q3'), 'the guide as an alternate forecast', ['g3'],\n   335\t                              scenario='alt'))\n   336\t    next(f for f in r1x['figures'] if f['id'] == 'dcq3')['inputs'] = ['altq3', 'mix']\n   337\t    item('R1bx', R1_FAMILY, R1_PASSAGES, r1x, lambda r: (any(c == 'C4' and 'another scenario' in d for c, d in r['errors']),\n   338\t                                                         'C4: the base reads an alternate scenario'), '')\n   339\t    r1x2 = r1('b')                                    # routed through an intermediate segment figure\n   340\t    r1x2['figures'].append(est('altq3', 108.0, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 Q3'), 'the guide as an alternate forecast', ['g3'],\n   341\t                               scenario='alt'))\n   342\t    r1x2['figures'].append(comp('altdc', 'share', ['altq3', 'mix'], 99.9, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', DC, 'FY2027 Q3 interim'), scenario='alt'))\n   343\t    next(f for f in r1x2['figures'] if f['id'] == 'dcq3').update(operation='product', inputs=['altdc', 'one'], value=99.9)\n   344\t    r1x2['figures'].append({'id': 'one', 'kind': 'estimate', 'unit': 'x', 'basis': 'forecast', 'what': W('NVIDIA', 'factor', DC, 'FY2027 Q3'),\n   345\t                            'basis_text': 'unchanged', 'rests_on': [], 'value': 1.0})\n   346\t    item('R1bx2', R1_FAMILY, R1_PASSAGES, r1x2, lambda r: (any(c == 'C4' and 'another scenario' in d for c, d in r['errors']),\n   347\t                                                           'C4: borrowed through an intermediate'), '')\n   348\t    r1x3 = r1('b')                                    # a point labelled range, read by the base\n   349\t    r1x3['figures'].append(est('altq3', 108.0, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027 Q3'), 'the guide as a point', ['g3'], scenario='range'))\n   350\t    next(f for f in r1x3['figures'] if f['id'] == 'dcq3')['inputs'] = ['altq3', 'mix']\n   351\t    item('R1bx3', R1_FAMILY, R1_PASSAGES, r1x3, lambda r: (any(c == 'C4' and 'range summary' in d for c, d in r['errors']),\n   352\t                                                           'C4: a point labelled range'), '')\n   353\t    p3e2 = copy.deepcopy(p3a)                         # the earlier forecast relabelled as an estimate\n   354\t    pri = next(f for f in p3e2['figures'] if f['id'] == 'pri')\n   355\t    pri.update(kind='estimate', basis_text='our earlier figure', rests_on=[])\n   356\t    p3e2['answers'][0]['outcome'] = 'pri'\n   357\t    p3e2['answers'][0]['reference'] = {'figure': 'gc392'}\n   358\t    item('P3e2', f1p, G_PASSAGES, p3e2, lambda r: (any(c == 'C10' for c, d in r['errors']), 'C10: an earlier forecast relabelled'), '')\n   359\t    p3e = copy.deepcopy(p3a)\n   360\t    p3e['answers'][0]['outcome'] = 'pri'\n   361\t    p3e['answers'][0]['reference'] = {'figure': 'gc392'}\n   362\t    item('P3e', f1p, G_PASSAGES, p3e, lambda r: (any(c == 'C10' and 'current outcome' in d for c, d in r['errors']), 'C10: a prior as the outcome'), '')\n   363\t    p3d = copy.deepcopy(p3a)\n   364\t    p3d['answers'][0]['reference'] = {'figure': 'pri', 'unavailable': 'no consensus supplied'}\n   365\t    item('P3d', f1p, G_PASSAGES, p3d, lambda r: (any(c == 'C5' and 'exactly one' in d for c, d in r['errors']), 'C5: both a figure and unavailable'), '')\n   366\t    p3c = copy.deepcopy(p3a)\n   367\t    next(f for f in p3c['figures'] if f['id'] == 'pri')['value'] = 431.0\n   368\t    item('P3c', f1p, G_PASSAGES, p3c, lambda r: ('C10' in codes(r), 'C10: a prior figure the earlier answer does not state'), '')\n   369\t    p3b = copy.deepcopy(c1)\n   370\t    p3b['figures'].append(est('wrap', 425.0, 'USD bn', W('NVIDIA', 'revenue', CO, 'FY2027'), 'our earlier forecast, close to the Street', ['gc392']))\n   371\t    p3b['answers'][0]['reference'] = {'figure': 'wrap'}\n   372\t    item('P3b', f1, G_PASSAGES, p3b, lambda r: (codes(r) == {'C5'}, 'C5 only'), '')\n   373\t\n   374\t    f3, c3 = g3()\n   375\t    p4 = copy.deepcopy(c3)\n272:                if rel == 'overlap_unknown' and fig.get('disputed') not in fig['inputs']:\n273:                    errors.append(('C8', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: overlap_unknown must name a disputed operand among its inputs'))\n285:            if rel == 'overlap_unknown' and fig.get('disputed') not in fig['inputs']:\n286:                errors.append(('C8', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: overlap_unknown must name a disputed operand among its inputs'))\n304:            if not bridge or bridge['kind'] != 'estimate' or set(bridge.get('converts', [])) != set(differing):\n305:                errors.append(('C8', f'{fig[\"id\"]}: converts {\", \".join(differing)} to {out[\"population\"]} {out[\"scope\"]} {out[\"period\"]} '\n409:            upstream = _upstream_of(f['id'], figs, refs)\n484:def _upstream_of(fid, figs, refs):\n499:    graph = [ref['id']] + sorted(_upstream_of(ref['id'], figs, refs))\n543:def _assumptions(family, figs, outcomes, calc, refs):\n549:        between = [f for f in [outcome_id] + sorted(_upstream_of(outcome_id, figs, refs)) if start in _upstream_of(f, figs, refs)]\n553:        if fig['kind'] == 'computed' and fig.get('relation') == 'overlap_unknown' and fig.get('disputed') in fig.get('inputs', []):\n554:            keep = [i for i in fig['inputs'] if i != fig['disputed']]\n555:            signs = [s for i, s in zip(fig['inputs'], fig.get('signs') or [1] * len(fig['inputs'])) if i != fig['disputed']]\n564:            if fig['id'] != outcome_id and fig['id'] not in _upstream_of(outcome_id, figs, refs):\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
