{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cat mutants.py | tail -82; nl -ba DESIGN.md | sed -n '74,84p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cat mutants.py | tail -82; nl -ba DESIGN.md | sed -n '74,84p'\"","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"Mutants of calc_check.py: each disables one rule on a scratch copy; the gate must miss the item that exercises it, and the\nunmutated control must pass. Harness-only. Usage: python3 mutants.py <scratch dir>  (writes the table to stdout).\"\"\"\nimport os\nimport shutil\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nMUTANTS = [\n    ('control (unmutated)', None, None, None),\n    ('C4 path rule off', \"bypass = [f for f in reachable(outcomes[view_id], stop=stop) if f not in stop and _key(figs[f]['what']) == want]\",\n     \"bypass = []\", 'R1b'),\n    ('C5 one-choice rule off', \"        if ('figure' in ref) == ('unavailable' in ref):\", \"        if False:\", 'P3d'),\n    ('scenario borrowing allowed', \"            borrowed = sorted(r for r in upstream if r in stop and figs[r].get('scenario', 'base') != sc)\", \"            borrowed = []\", 'G2x'),\n    ('range summary not validated', \"        if f['kind'] != 'estimate' or 'low' not in f or 'high' not in f or f['id'] not in outcome_ids or readers:\", \"        if False:\", 'R1bx3'),\n    ('prior status from label only', \"        earlier = fig['kind'] == 'prior' or fig.get('basis') == 'prior_forecast' or 'pointer' in fig\", \"        earlier = fig['kind'] == 'prior'\", 'P3e2'),\n    ('prior as outcome allowed', \"        if owners:                                    # [46h.2] nor the current outcome\", \"        if False:\", 'P3e'),\n    ('C3 off', \"if plo > wlo + 1e-9 or phi > whi + 1e-9:\", \"if False:\", 'R1a'),\n    ('C1 accepts any substring (alone)', \"matches = [e for e in extract(passage['text']) if e['text'] == fig.get('expression')]\",\n     \"matches = [e for e in extract(passage['text']) if fig.get('expression') in e['text']]\", 'T9'),\n    ('C5 allows estimates', \"if any(n['kind'] in ('estimate', 'prior') or n['basis'] in ('forecast', 'prior_forecast') for n in nodes):\",\n     \"if any(n['kind'] == 'prior' for n in nodes):\", 'P3b'),\n    ('per-unit identity ignores scope', \"same = all((i['what']['population'], i['what']['scope']) == (out['population'], out['scope']) for i in ins)\",\n     \"same = True\", 'P4'),\n    ('per-unit inverse loses its scale', \"            lo, hi = lo / 1e9, hi / 1e9\", \"            pass\", 'G3inv'),\n    ('C2 tolerance 50%', \"return abs(declared - expected) <= max(0.005 * abs(expected), floor)\",\n     \"return abs(declared - expected) <= max(0.5 * abs(expected), floor)\", 'P2'),\n    ('bound direction ignored', \"        if want is not None and have != want:\", \"        if want is not None and have is None:\", 'R4m'),\n    ('C9 same base off (both clauses)', \"        if rel['type'] != 'same_base' or rel['later'] not in outcomes\", \"        if True or rel['later'] not in outcomes\", 'G4m'),\n    ('C10 prior not authenticated', \"        if ans_prior.get('day') != ptr.get('day') or not any(_same(fig.get('value'), v) for v in ans_prior.get('values', [])):\",\n     \"        if False:\", 'P3c'),\n]\n\n\ndef main(scratch):\n    scratch = Path(scratch)\n    src = (HERE / 'calc_check.py').read_text()\n    gate = (HERE / 'gate.py').read_text().replace('REPO = HERE.parents[2]', f\"REPO = Path('{HERE.parents[2]}')\")\n    print('mutant | expected miss | result')\n    failed = 0\n    for name, old, new, target in MUTANTS:\n        if old is not None and src.count(old) != 1:\n            print(f'{name} | {target} | MUTATION SITE NOT FOUND ONCE')\n            failed += 1\n            continue\n        folder = scratch / name.replace(' ', '_').replace('(', '').replace(')', '')\n        folder.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        (folder / 'calc_check.py').write_text(src if old is None else src.replace(old, new))\n        (folder / 'gate.py').write_text(gate.replace('HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent', f\"HERE = Path('{folder}')\"))\n        run = subprocess.run([sys.executable, 'gate.py'], cwd=folder, capture_output=True, text=True, env={**os.environ, 'PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE': '1'})\n        misses = run.stdout.split('misses:')[-1].strip().splitlines()[0] if 'misses:' in run.stdout else f'no output: {run.stderr.strip()[-200:]}'\n        if target is None:\n            ok = run.returncode == 0\n            print(f'{name} | none | {\"PASS\" if ok else \"BROKEN\"} ({misses})')\n        else:\n            ok = run.returncode == 1 and f\"'{target}'\" in misses\n            print(f'{name} | {target} | {\"CAUGHT\" if ok else \"NOT CAUGHT\"} ({misses})')\n        failed += not ok\n    shutil.rmtree(scratch, ignore_errors=True)\n    return 1 if failed else 0\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    if len(sys.argv) != 2 or sys.argv[1].startswith('-'):\n        raise SystemExit('usage: mutants.py <scratch dir>')\n    raise SystemExit(main(sys.argv[1]))\n    74\t| **C4 one forecast per shared quantity** [46b.1, 46c.1] | for each shared quantity and period the declaration names, each scenario has exactly one `basis: forecast` node. **Every path** in the graph from a member's outcome to any figure that measures that quantity and period passes through that node. A guide, consensus or other source of a future period may feed the forecast node; no path from an outcome may reach it while avoiding the node | the $108B guide feeding v14's $113.5B forecast and, on another path, v9's Data Center Q3 directly: the same guide node, a bypass |\n    75\t| **C5 reference** [46b.3, 46c.1] | each answer's reference is `unavailable` with a reason, or a direct `source` figure of basis consensus, guidance or third_party from a passage whose speaker is not the system, or a `computed` figure whose whole graph is computed figures over such sources and `reported` sources (q02: $392B consensus × 92% reported mix). No `estimate`, `forecast` or `prior_forecast` anywhere in the reference's graph. Its provenance is shown | the system's own forecast presented as the market's, directly or wrapped in an estimate that cites outside evidence |\n    76\t| **C6 rung and outcome** [46.2] | the chosen rung's band overlaps the outcome (a point: contains it). The reasons say why that band, where the range overlaps several | a rung no part of the outcome falls in |\n    77\t| **C7 structure** [46.5] | exactly one answer per member; an answer's outcome `what` matches its member's question (population, measure, scope, period, from the question's typed key); figure ids are unique; references are not dangling and not circular; operations come from the closed set | a missing or doubled member, a borrowed outcome, a dangling or circular figure |\n    78\t| **C8 operand compatibility** [46b.3] | by operation. **sum/difference:** same measure, population and scope, with periods either disjoint and together forming the output period (`time_aggregation`), or identical with a declared relation (`accounting_parts` needs a declared `part_of`). **roll_forward:** an opening balance as of a date, and flows over a period starting then or later, give the closing balance [46c.2]. **per unit** [gate run 1]: a total over a price per unit gives units, and units times that price give the total, for one population and scope (q19's $20B at $5,000 a Vera CPU is four million units). **share:** numerator and denominator stated, with a declared `part_of` or a reported mix. **product/ratio:** a change of measure, population, scope or period not covered above needs a bridge estimate whose `converts` names the actual operands, and an assumption | 730/800 × $1.3T with no bridge naming e1786's four-company 2026 spending and e2535's five-company capex; a bridge that converts other operands |\n    79\t\n    80\t| **C4 scenarios** [46g.3, 46h.1, 46i.1] | each scenario has one forecast node per shared quantity. Scenario membership is derived along the whole path: no figure of a point scenario may depend, at any depth, on a forecast node of another scenario. A `range` summary is an estimate with low and high, is an answer's outcome, and feeds no figure; only it may rest on several scenarios; a bypass is a path that reaches the quantity through no forecast node of any scenario | a low path on the high total; a guide relabelled as an alternate scenario and read by the base |\n    81\t| **C5 one choice** [46g.2] | a reference names exactly one of a figure or `unavailable` | a prior figure hidden beside an \"unavailable\" reason |\n    82\t| **C9 same base** [46f.3] | for each `same_base(later, earlier)`, the later member's outcome rests on the earlier member's outcome, and every path from it to a figure of the earlier member's quantity and period passes through that outcome | FY2028 grown from the $392B consensus instead of q01's $400–435B forecast |\n    83\t| **C10 earlier forecasts** [46f.3, 46f.4, 46h.2, 46i.2] | a figure is an earlier forecast when its kind is prior, its basis is prior_forecast or it carries a pointer (derived, not labelled), and it must then be kind prior with basis prior_forecast; such a figure points to an earlier answer shown in the request and equals a figure that answer states; it feeds no figure and is no answer's outcome | an invented or misdated earlier figure; an earlier forecast used as an input |\n    84\t| **C2 bound direction** [46f.3] | for positive operands, a result's bound side follows its inputs: sums and products keep a lower or upper side, a ratio's or difference's second operand flips it, and mixed sides give `approx` | \"more than double\" times $20B declared below $40B |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
