{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"agent_message","text":"GATE FAIL\n\n- **Scenario names can still hide the original contradiction.** I replayed R1 with company revenue in `base` and Data Center in `alt`. Both checks accepted $146B for Data Center against $127B for the whole company, along with the original $108B and $113.5B Q3 bases. A G2x variant also passed by crossing the nonshared segment-share forecasts. Check every upstream forecast, including nonshared inputs, and require related published outcomes to cover the same scenarios. [Scenario checks](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:373)\n- **The range rule conflicts with the gold’s same-base reasoning.** Combining G2 and G4, q22 was refused by C4 when it used q01’s published FY2027 range and by C9 when it used the two forecast paths behind that range. Make C9 check that each later scenario uses the earlier forecast feeding the corresponding end of the published range. Keep the range summary as the published answer. [C4 and C9](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:351) · [q22 gold reasoning](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/gold-v1.json:982)\n- **An earlier forecast can still become the current answer.** A P3e variant passed both checks with the same $425B as a fresh `estimate`, even though its explanation explicitly said it reused the earlier forecast unchanged. The checker only sees the structured markers the model supplies. Keep earlier forecast figures out of the calculation request and use them for comparison after the current calculation is fixed. [C10](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/calc_check.py:427) · [Request renderer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/render_v13.py:100)"}}
